      <p>Buying a tiny home is not like buying a regular house. There is often no real estate agent, no standard inspection, no appraisal and no title company checking the details, and a tiny house on wheels may be legally closer to an RV than a home. That puts more of the homework on you. Whether you are wondering how to buy a tiny home outright or how to get a tiny home by building one, the seven steps below cover it in order.</p>

